<title>NIGERIA: Nigerian forex demand shots up after budget.</title>
<headline>Nigerian forex demand shots up after budget.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's central bank said on Monday that it sold $59.5 million at 80 naira to the dollar during its weekly auction.</p>
<p>The previous week, the bank sold $887,494 at the same rate as most banks shunned the auction in anticipation of changes to the forex regime and the fiscal 1997 budget.</p>
<p>&quot;The auction market is back to normal now that there has been no change in the foreign exchange rate,&quot; said one banker.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
</text>
